+## 3. Switches (documented in `docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md`)
+
+| switch | default | meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `GGML_VK_STAGING_RESERVE` | device-probed: `suballocation_block_size` (1 GiB here) | bytes reserved on the staging heap before any bulk admission; `0` disables, unparsable keeps the default |
+| `GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MAX` | derived: free bytes on the heaps carrying this batch's host candidates, after the staging reserve and live bytes | cap on one load's host-split bytes; `0` forbids host placement |
+
+Both are read from the environment at runtime (`ggml_vk_env_bytes`), never compile-only. The reserve
+default is a real requirement, not a guess: a bulk weight buffer is capped at
+`suballocation_block_size`, one tensor lives inside one such buffer, and `sync_staging` is sized to
+one copy — so that block size is the largest single upload chunk this device can be asked to stage.
